@EndToEnd
Feature: Golden vectors are read-only and independently sourced

  Scenario: The first vector file carries reference-run provenance and matches the reference
    Given the vector file "tests/fixtures/verify/adler32.vectors.json"
    When I run "integrity check"
    Then the exit code is 0
    And the file's provenance kind is "reference-run" with source "python" and generatedBy "python"
    And its vector "abc" has input text "abc" and expected hex "024D0127"
    And the python reference "zlib.adler32(b'abc')" prints 38600999

  Scenario: An edited expected value is detected
    Given a sealed tree whose vector "abc" expects hex "024D0127"
    And the expected value is edited to "024D0128" without sealing
    When I run "integrity check"
    Then the exit code is 1
    And stderr contains "PLY0027: golden file 'tests/fixtures/verify/adler32.vectors.json' was modified: hash differs from the golden lock"

  Scenario: Vectors generated by Polypiler itself are refused
    Given a vector file whose provenance has generatedBy "polypiler"
    When I run "integrity seal" on it
    Then the exit code is 1
    And stderr contains "PLY0028"
    And golden.lock.json is unchanged

  Scenario: A vector change in the same commit as compiler code is refused
    Given a git history where commit "c2" changes "tests/fixtures/verify/adler32.vectors.json" and "Polypiler.Core.IR/Module.cs"
    And the vector file is sealed and golden.changes.md has its line
    When I run "integrity check --base c1"
    Then the exit code is 1
    And stderr contains "PLY0027"
    And stderr contains "changed together with 'Polypiler.Core.IR/Module.cs'"

  Scenario: A declared, isolated vector change passes
    Given a git history where commit "c2" changes only "tests/fixtures/verify/adler32.vectors.json", "tests/fixtures/golden.lock.json" and "tests/fixtures/golden.changes.md"
    And golden.changes.md gained "- tests/fixtures/verify/adler32.vectors.json: add 'a' vector (source: python)"
    When I run "integrity check --base c1"
    Then the exit code is 0

  Scenario: An upstream-embedded source must be in the corpus lock
    Given a vector file with provenance kind "upstream-embedded" whose source names the pinned "Hawkynt/Hawkynt.github.io" commit and the path "Cipher/algorithms/checksum/nothing.js"
    When I run "integrity check"
    Then the exit code is 1
    And stderr contains "PLY0028"
    And stderr contains "source is not in the corpus lock"
